Place the Raspberry Pi OS Lite base image (.img.xz) to build from here.

FullPageOS builds on Raspberry Pi OS Lite, Debian 13 "Trixie". The pinned
release URLs and sha256 checksums per architecture are defined in
src/config (FULLPAGEOS_IMAGE_URL_ARM64 / FULLPAGEOS_IMAGE_URL_ARMHF and
FULLPAGEOS_IMAGE_SHA256_*). Download the image for the architecture you
are building and verify it, e.g.:

    cd src/image
    source ../config
    wget "$FULLPAGEOS_IMAGE_URL_ARM64"
    echo "$FULLPAGEOS_IMAGE_SHA256_ARM64  $(basename "$FULLPAGEOS_IMAGE_URL_ARM64")" | sha256sum -c

(Use the _ARMHF variables for a 32-bit build. The official checksum is
also published next to each image as <image-url>.sha256.)

If not otherwise specified, CustomPiOS uses the most recent Raspberry Pi
OS file matching *-raspios*.{zip,7z,xz} in this directory, so keep only
the image for the architecture you are building — or set BASE_ZIP_IMG
(via src/config.local or the environment) to the exact file to use.

Always pin a dated release plus its sha256; never build from an undated
*_latest download.
